WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.710
A skater turns slowly on the
ice, arms stretched wide.

2
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.540
She draws her arms in tight to her body.

3
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:12.320
And she whirls faster and faster,
until she is almost a blur.

4
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:15.530
Spinning faster seems
to need something extra.

5
00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.290
So where does the extra spin come from?

6
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.220
Her muscles?

7
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:20.120
The ice?

8
00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.060
The air?

9
00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.620
Something else?

10
00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:25.420
In this mission, you'll
meet angular momentum,

11
00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:29.340
and see how a turning force
acting for a time changes it.

12
00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:32.960
Then you'll drop a still disc
onto a spinning turntable,

13
00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.200
and work out how fast
the pair turns together.

14
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.520
Your mission: explain where the
skater's extra spin comes from.
